# HUD lag off. Status: used in every headset session since build 33 (session logs). Without it the visor floats on a plane in front of the player, on a single axis.
# CSamusHudMP1::UpdateHudLag (main+0xcaf1d8): the game's "HUD Lag" option (gameState+0x14d) sends the HUD camera through
# ApplyClassicLag, which lags it behind the first-person camera's rotation; with the head in that camera, the visor
# swings behind every head turn. This takes the no-lag branch always (the GUI camera = screen shake only); the
# player's option and the save are untouched.
# main+0xcaf1dc: cbz w8,#0xcaf440 (28 13 00 34) -> b #0xcaf440 (99 00 00 14).
# Expect at 0xcaf1d0: 08 4D 43 F9 08 01 40 F9 08 35 45 39 28 13 00 34
# The launcher's mode C staging copies it into the build's load dir as @enabled.
@flag offset_shift 0x100
@enabled
00CAF1DC 99000014
@stop
